.TH SDL_RunApp 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_RunApp \- Initializes and launches an SDL application, by doing platform-specific initialization before calling your mainFunction and cleanups after it returns, if that is needed for a specific platform, otherwise it just calls mainFunction.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_main.h>
.PP
.BI "int SDL_RunApp(int argc, char *argv[], SDL_main_func mainFunction, void *reserved);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
You can use this if you want to use your own main() implementation without using
.BR SDL_main
(like when using
.BR SDL_MAIN_HANDLED )\[char46]
When using this, you do
.IR not
need
.BR SDL_SetMainReady ()\[char46]
.PP
If
.BR argv
is NULL, SDL will provide command line arguments, either by querying the OS for them if possible, or supplying a filler array if not\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I argc
the argc parameter from the application\(aqs main() function, or 0 if the platform\(aqs main-equivalent has no argc\[char46]
.TP
.I argv
the argv parameter from the application\(aqs main() function, or NULL if the platform\(aqs main-equivalent has no argv\[char46]
.TP
.I mainFunction
your SDL app\(aqs C-style main()\[char46] NOT the function you\(aqre calling this from! Its name doesn\(aqt matter; it doesn\(aqt literally have to be
.BR main \[char46]

.TP
.I reserved
should be NULL (reserved for future use, will probably be platform-specific then)\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the return value from mainFunction: 0 on success, otherwise failure;
.BR SDL_GetError ()
might have more information on the failure\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
Generally this is called once, near startup, from the process\(aqs initial thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

